# 🐳️ The build context of `Dockerfile` beside this file (BuildKit prefers `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the root
# `.dockerignore`): nothing but what the proctor build reads. Cargo needs the manifest of every workspace member, the
# lock file of the proctor's workspace and the Rust sources; the image carries the quiz content and the stack files.
# Everything else in the repository — the web code, the assets, the documents — stays out, so the context is small and
# the compile layer survives every change that is not Rust. The exclusions after the admissions win over them:
# host-local state and build output hold Rust files too.
*
!Cargo.toml
!🎓️teaching/Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!.cargo
!**/Cargo.toml
!**/*.rs
!🎓️teaching/**/❓️quiz/🔣️.json
!🎓️teaching/🏛️architecture/❓️quiz/🚀️deploy/compose.yaml
!🎓️teaching/🏛️architecture/❓️quiz/🚀️deploy/Caddyfile
.git
.jj
.nx
.venv
.🧬semio
.tmp*
**/node_modules
**/target
**/🎯️target
**/🎯️target-*
**/📤️dist
**/dist
**/pkg
**/temp
**/🗑️generated
♻️mit-bestand/🔎️recherche
